  "live_records": {
    "q-154716": {
      "dom_id": "step-q154716",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/0c5a57e090562c65ff7f0ff8d7c63f469a038d4396bba68be3cb4916f4e7aab7.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $\\overset{^}{COE}?$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/18be9d5946a70aa62b4dda5408fa7e3312fe2e33675cbf695cbbdecac2feaa5b.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $\\overset{^}{COD}$ and $\\overset{^}{DOE}$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OD}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\\overset{^}{COE} & =m\\overset{^}{COD}+m\\overset{^}{DOE} \\\\  & ={70}^{∘}+{35}^{∘} \\\\  & ={105}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
