    "q-21727": {
      "dom_id": "step-q21727",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/bd99171c2696038851bf0fdf7297d2e4a60791f6b11083af8cd51baf48930b2d.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $\\overset{^}{COE}?$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/67952e3c3d8b030327cbae686da23d466d509de9171242f5ccc4e502f10813d7.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $\\overset{^}{COD}$ and $\\overset{^}{DOE}$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OD}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\\overset{^}{COE} & =m\\overset{^}{COD}+m\\overset{^}{DOE} \\\\  & ={63}^{∘}+{47}^{∘} \\\\  & ={110}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
