    "q-53142": {
      "dom_id": "step-q53142",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/7e365bb8c51729748b0efdb54f50459859a382cba1def4b32b4009b3bde89dbd.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠COE.$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/ae007a68607a96bfd78986eeae11e69a4c8bd8dba35e8997933885d2ff1dc29f.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠COD$ and $∠DOE$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{OD}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠COE & =m∠COD+m∠DOE \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}+{59}^{∘} \\\\  & ={104}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
