    "q-150770": {
      "dom_id": "step-q150770",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/51504155eb8a1886004062bc3f14845119f2e8f669273aece8cf4772c9a51d42.png)\n\nThe measure of the angle $∠LON$ is ${120}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠MON.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠LOM$ and $∠MON$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{OM}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠LON)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠LOM$ and $∠MON).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠MON$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠LON)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠LOM).$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx={120}^{∘}-{50}^{∘}={70}^{∘}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
