    "q-4320": {
      "dom_id": "step-q4320",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/1ed3b825702e9d446754d5bf56ff2964f8456bce45ab57fe9f6931458c9f5038.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠DEA={147}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠CED.$\n\nThe measure of $∠CED$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠DEA)$ and the two smaller known angles $(∠CEB$ and $∠BEA).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx={147}^{∘}-{56}^{∘}-{40}^{∘}={51}^{∘}.\n$$",
