      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/cb84da67a9f114bf78347f1e2ba7f7c1f4a31c632733a942200fe2fde208b61c.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠AFE={144}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠DFE.$\n\nThe measure of $∠DFE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠AFE)$ and the two smaller known angles $(∠CFD$ and $∠AFC).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx={144}^{∘}-{82}^{∘}-{25}^{∘}={37}^{∘}.\n$$",
