      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14131900/assets/1650402ae8691f2578dc491516b074c20759afc0a6b848e003c03bad104fa8a5.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠AFE={155}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠DFE.$\n\nThe measure of $∠DFE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠AFE)$ and the two smaller known angles $(∠AFC$ and $∠CFD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx={155}^{∘}-{46}^{∘}-{65}^{∘}={44}^{∘}.\n$$",
